# Invariant: the file-size baseline is GENERATED, never merged.
#
# `.filesize-baseline.json` is rewritten wholesale by
# `pnpm audit:filesize:update` (scripts/check-file-size.ts). Every refactor wave
# removes the files it fixed, so concurrent branches routinely touch it. A
# textual 3-way merge of a generated JSON file produces a syntactically valid but
# semantically wrong hybrid — a stale entry silently re-grandfathers a file that
# is already fixed, which is exactly the drift the ratchet exists to prevent.
#
# `-merge` makes git report a conflict and leave OUR version in the tree instead
# of inventing that hybrid.
#
# Deliberately NOT `-diff`: marking it binary would hide the one thing a reviewer
# of a refactor-wave PR needs to see — exactly which files that wave retired from
# the baseline. The one-time cost is a 138-line diff in the commit that
# introduces the file.
#
# Resolve a conflict by regenerating, never by editing conflict markers:
#
#   git checkout origin/main -- .filesize-baseline.json
#   pnpm audit:filesize:update
#   pnpm audit:filesize:check
#
# Regeneration is self-checking: a stale key that no longer exceeds the ceiling
# fails the gate's RETIRED mode anyway.
.filesize-baseline.json -merge

# Same contract for the function-size baseline, regenerated by
# `pnpm audit:funcsize:update` (scripts/check-function-size.ts).
.funcsize-baseline.json -merge
